course: dictionary
lesson: 14580
title: Placate: calming someone down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To placate someone is to make them feel less angry or upset. You might do it with a kind word, a gift or a helpful action. «The crying toddler stopped when his mum gave him a biscuit.» The biscuit was a way to placate him, because it calmed him down.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Sam was furious that his game was broken, so Dad promised to fix it and placated him.» Furious means very angry, and Dad did something kind to help. So placate must mean to calm him down. Check it: "Dad calmed him down" still makes sense, so you have got it.
explain: Placate is a verb, so it changes form: placates, placated and placating. «Yesterday the waiter placated the angry customer with a free drink.» Waiters often placate customers when something goes wrong.
explain: Myths and history use this word too. «The villagers brought food and gold to placate the angry god.» They wanted the god to be calmer and less cross. Similar words are calm, soothe and pacify, but placate often means calming someone by giving them something or saying something kind.
fact: Placate means to make someone feel less angry or upset.
fact: You can placate someone by giving them something, or by saying something kind.
fact: Placate is a verb: placates, placated and placating are its other forms.
fact: Similar words include calm, soothe and pacify.
fact: In old stories, people tried to placate gods with gifts so the gods would not be cross.
exercise: «Mum gave the crying baby her favourite toy to placate him.» What does placate mean here? | To wake him up | *To make him feel less upset | To make him cry louder
exercise: «The customer was furious, so the manager placated her with a free meal.» Find and copy one word that shows the customer was angry. | free | *furious | manager | meal
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to placate? | tease | ignore | *soothe | shout
test: «The gods were angry, so the people brought gifts to placate them.» Why did the people bring gifts? | To make the gods angrier | *To make the gods less angry | To make the gods go away for ever
test: Sam is placating his little brother after their fight, and his brother is upset. What is Sam doing? | Leaving the room to play | *Trying to calm his brother down | Ignoring his brother completely | Making his brother angrier
exam: Which sentence shows someone placating another person? | The coach forgot the name of the player | The teacher shouted at the upset class | *Dad calmed the cross toddler down with a hug | Dad ran out of the room and slammed the door
